    "created_at": "2016-06-09T01:25:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-09T01:25:00Z",
    "body": "attr() should work exactly as attribute selectors, and I just fixed that in the spec. CSS defers case-sensitivity to the host language, so HTML just needs to say that attribute names are case-sensitive, or Unicode case-folded, or ASCII case-insensitive, or whatever it wants to say about that. Calling out individual CSS features and defining their matching behavior individually seems like a bad way to do this. :(\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/224778234/reactions",
